      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lena was originally known as Maple Valley and owes its location to the expanding railroad network in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lena%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village of Lena was named after Helena Louisa McCartney, the future wife of Oconto Postmaster George R. Hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lena%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "French-Canadian immigrants settled the area in the late 1870s to establish small-scale logging operations along Jones Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lena_town_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lena celebrates its farming history every September with an annual event called Dairyfest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
